# 27. Five Required Validation Prompts

The system must support the following five manual validation prompts through ADK Web.

## Prompt 1 — Baseline

```text
Design a production-ready order management architecture
supporting 10,000 concurrent users.

Include customer, order, product, order status,
database, API, scalability, caching, and failure handling.

Do not use previous assumptions or learned knowledge.
Provide your best initial architecture.

This is a baseline benchmark.
```

Record:

```text
answer
evaluation
strategy
workflow
agents
duration
```

---

## Prompt 2 — Learning Reuse

```text
Design a production-ready commerce architecture
supporting 20,000 concurrent users.

Include customer, order, payment, shipping,
inventory, database, scalability, caching,
messaging, and failure handling.

Use relevant experiences, lessons, strategies,
agent performance, and workflow knowledge from
previous tasks if available.

At the end, identify which previous knowledge
influenced your decisions.
```

Validate:

```text
lesson retrieval
strategy reuse
workflow reuse
agent selection
answer quality
```

---

## Prompt 3 — Critic and Improvement

```text
Consider the following architecture for an order system
supporting 100,000 concurrent users:

All services share one relational database.
All requests are synchronous.
Order, payment, inventory, and shipping are tightly coupled.

Evaluate this architecture.

Identify scalability, availability, performance,
coupling, and failure-handling problems.

If the architecture is inadequate, use the critic and
improvement workflow to produce a better architecture.

Record what was wrong with the original approach
and what was improved.
```

Validate:

```text
Critic
Improvement
Retry
Final evaluation
Lesson generation
```

---

## Prompt 4 — New Session Persistence

Start a new ADK Web session.

```text
Design a scalable order processing system supporting
100,000 concurrent users.

Compare:

1. Shared database architecture
2. Database-per-service architecture

Use previous lessons and historical strategy/workflow
performance if available.

Explain why the selected approach is better.
```

Validate that knowledge survives:

```text
new ADK session
agent restart
application restart
```

---

## Prompt 5 — Full Continuous Improvement

```text
Design a production-ready order management platform
supporting 100,000 concurrent users.

The platform must support:

- Customer
- Product
- Order
- Payment
- Inventory
- Shipping
- Notifications
- Order tracking

Use historical experiences and lessons.

Select the strategy with the best historical performance
for this type of task.

Select the workflow with the best historical performance.

Select appropriate specialized agents.

Critically evaluate the generated solution.

If weaknesses are found, improve the solution.

At the end, provide a validation summary containing:

1. Selected workflow
2. Selected strategy
3. Selected agents
4. Retrieved lessons
5. Whether critic was invoked
6. Whether improvement was required
7. Whether retry occurred
8. Final evaluation
9. New lesson generated
10. Historical knowledge that influenced the result
```

