# 30. Acceptance Criteria

Phase 6 is complete only when all of the following are demonstrated.

### AC-01 — Baseline

The system can execute a benchmark with isolated/empty historical knowledge.

### AC-02 — Persistence

Experiences, evaluations, lessons, strategies, agent performance, and workflow performance survive application and ADK session restart.

### AC-03 — Learning

The system generates reusable lessons from evaluated experiences.

### AC-04 — Retrieval

Relevant lessons can be retrieved for later tasks.

### AC-05 — Strategy Adaptation

Historical strategy performance influences future strategy selection.

### AC-06 — Workflow Adaptation

Historical workflow performance influences future workflow selection.

### AC-07 — Agent Adaptation

Historical agent performance can influence future agent selection.

### AC-08 — Critic

The system can identify weaknesses in an answer.

### AC-09 — Improvement

The system can produce an improved answer after criticism.

### AC-10 — Generalization

A learned lesson can influence a related but differently worded task.

### AC-11 — New Session

Learning remains available in a new ADK Web session.

### AC-12 — Restart

Learning remains available after restarting the application.

### AC-13 — Measurement

Baseline and post-learning metrics are automatically recorded.

### AC-14 — Comparison

The system can compare baseline and post-learning benchmark results.

### AC-15 — Visualization

Streamlit displays the complete continuous-improvement trace.

### AC-16 — Graph

GraphQLite shows the relationships between task, experience, evaluation, lesson, strategy, workflow, and agents.

### AC-17 — Failure Isolation

Failure of evaluation, learning, or visualization must not prevent the main agent from answering the user.

### AC-18 — No False Improvement

The system must not claim improvement merely because a lesson was retrieved.

Actual task/evaluation metrics must support the claim.

### AC-19 — No Self-Modifying Code

The system must NOT modify:

```text
source code
agent prompts
Python files
workflow definitions
strategy implementation
```

Improvement must occur through learned data and controlled configuration.

### AC-20 — No Infinite Learning

Learning must occur only as a consequence of:

```text
real task
benchmark task
explicit developer test
```

There must be no autonomous infinite learning loop.

