# 32. Final Definition of Success

The Self-Improving Agent will be considered successfully validated when the system demonstrates this complete cycle:

```text
             EXPERIENCE
                  ↓
             EVALUATION
                  ↓
               LESSON
                  ↓
              MEMORY
                  ↓
             RETRIEVAL
                  ↓
          STRATEGY SELECTION
                  ↓
          WORKFLOW SELECTION
                  ↓
            AGENT SELECTION
                  ↓
               SOLUTION
                  ↓
               CRITIC
                  ↓
             IMPROVEMENT
                  ↓
             NEW RESULT
                  ↓
             NEW EVALUATION
                  ↓
        MEASURABLE IMPROVEMENT
```

The most important acceptance condition is:

> **A future benchmark result must demonstrate measurable improvement compared with the baseline, while the system can provide a trace showing which learned experiences, lessons, strategies, workflows, or agent-performance information caused the change.**

